30,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"My findings are sobering. While our water-based infrastructure has held up, our surfacing is a disaster, and our tree planting failed miserably due to poor aftercare.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"The ground is a risk. Firms are warning about clay subsoil and slippage, though small-scale work is fine. Also, we can't hoard the center or gate without closing the park.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,1,talk,Mio,,"Oh wow! I found out that planting and water management are way more expensive to maintain than hard surfaces. Plus, the habitat fund only pays for the green stuff!","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"Our internal staff is depleted. We've lost over half our groundskeepers. We rely on contractors for specialist care, though we have some volunteers for habitats and sports.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,1,talk,Minako,,"The site is under pressure. People mostly use the firm ground to reach the tram, and our drainage is failing, while the heat in the open areas is becoming extreme.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Misaki, if the center is a bottleneck for construction, we should avoid any plan that requires massive central excavation.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Benjamin, I agree. The clay subsoil makes any deep digging a gamble. Shallow work is safer and more predictable.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,2,talk,Mio,,"@Asuka, if we don't have enough staff, maybe we should pick something that doesn't need a ton of gardening? The upkeep costs for plants are scary!","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Mio, that is a logical point. We have volunteers for specific tasks, but the general roll is too short to handle a high-maintenance landscape.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,2,talk,Minako,,"@Benjamin, the drainage issues and heat readings suggest that simply paving everything over might worsen the environment, even if it's easier to maintain.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Minako, a fair point. However, the record shows that our ""green"" attempts often die from neglect. We need a balance of utility and survival.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,3,talk,Misaki,,"@Minako, the weekday crossing data is key. People want a direct, firm path to the tram. Any plan that forces them into mud or reeds will fail.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,3,talk,Mio,,"But the habitat fund is so much money! It would be a shame to ignore it, as long as we can afford to keep it later.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Mio, the fund pays for the build, but the city pays for the upkeep. With only seven groundskeepers left, we cannot afford a ""beautiful"" mistake.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,3,talk,Minako,,"Exactly. We need something that handles the water, provides shade for the heat, but respects the flow of the commuters.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"It seems we are searching for a solution that is structurally shallow, operationally lean, and environmentally functional.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,4,talk,Misaki,,And one that doesn't require us to shut down the main gate for months.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,4,talk,Mio,,I just hope we don't pick something that bankrupts the maintenance budget in three years!,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,4,talk,Asuka,,I agree. The human capacity to maintain the park is our tightest constraint.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,4,pass,Minako,,Over,"{""forced"":false,""empty"":false}"
50,3,,status,Mio,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
51,3,,status,Misaki,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
52,3,,status,Benjamin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
53,3,,status,Minako,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
54,3,,status,Asuka,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
55,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"The candidates are Market Plaza, Woodland Walk, Wetland Restoration, and Sports Terraces. Given the failure of previous plantings, Woodland Walk seems a risky gamble.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,1,talk,Misaki,,"Market Plaza and Sports Terraces involve surfacing. Wetland Restoration requires significant earth-moving and drainage changes, which the firms warned about.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,1,talk,Mio,,"Market Plaza is hard-surfaced, which is cheaper to maintain! But Wetland Restoration fits the habitat fund perfectly. I'm torn.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,1,talk,Asuka,,Sports Terraces would utilize the youth league volunteers. Market Plaza is lean. Woodland Walk and Wetland Restoration require specialist care we no longer have.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,1,talk,Minako,,Market Plaza addresses the heat with shade and the tram commuters with firm ground. Wetland Restoration addresses the drainage but might obstruct the crossings.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Asuka, the Sports Terraces' surfacing would likely end up patched and broken like the civic hall apron. Market Plaza is more flexible.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Minako, Market Plaza is the safest for the ground. It's shallow work. Wetland Restoration is a nightmare for clay subsoil and slippage.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,2,talk,Mio,,"@Benjamin, if we go with Market Plaza, we lose the habitat fund money. But if we go with Wetland, the upkeep costs will be triple!","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Mio, the upkeep is the priority. Market Plaza is the most sustainable for our current staffing levels.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,2,talk,Minako,,I agree. Market Plaza provides the shade we need for the August heat and keeps the tram path clear.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,The logic is consistent. Market Plaza avoids the biological volatility of the Woodland and the structural risks of the Wetland.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,3,talk,Misaki,,It also avoids the hoarding issues of the center if we phase the stall infrastructure correctly.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,3,talk,Mio,,I guess the long-term budget is more important than the initial grant. I'm starting to lean toward the Plaza.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,3,talk,Asuka,,It is the only choice that doesn't assume we have a workforce that doesn't exist.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,3,talk,Minako,,It is the most pragmatic response to the actual behavior of the people and the land.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,I am satisfied. Market Plaza is the most rational choice. I vote for Market Plaza.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,4,talk,Misaki,,I agree. It minimizes the risk of slippage and delivery delays. I vote for Market Plaza.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,4,talk,Mio,,Okay! Let's save the maintenance budget. I vote for Market Plaza!,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,4,talk,Asuka,,"For the sake of the staff and the rota, I vote for Market Plaza.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,4,talk,Minako,,It fits the usage patterns and the climate needs. I vote for Market Plaza.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
